The following packages were ported from it:

- desktop/internal/term        from internal/term (the screen and its encoders)
- desktop/internal/localshell  from internal/localshell (the local shell on a pty)
- desktop/internal/shellkind   from internal/shellkind (shell detection)
- desktop/internal/termview    from internal/workbench (the terminal view: the row cache,
                               output pump, painting, selection, input and scrollbar)

Changes: import paths were moved into this module. The terminal view keeps only a local
shell in one pane; Motty's SSH, AI, recording, prediction, links, find, toolbar and
multi-pane parts were left out, and its state, session and terminal types were merged into
one View.

The port was taken from Motty at 8958a472. These later Motty changes were taken since,
adapted to the merged View:

- 3a2b91dc  output keeps the selection on its text; here the screen counts buffer
            generations and the view clears or trims the selection when it sees one change
- c3cc6f6c  rows are painted with a stable text identity, so their textures are reused
            as the rows scroll
- 546e40ae  Ctrl+C is turned back on for the shell when Lithe inherited it turned off
- dbd2a6f2  Clear sends PowerShell a form feed; here only when the shell runs no program
- 2f73c352  the Microsoft Store PowerShell 7 alias is found and preferred
- 02916ed5  PowerShell keeps its version banner
- d0759bb3  a drag with Alt (Ctrl+Alt on Linux) selects a block of columns, copied
            line by line
- 4116260e  Find opens with the selected text of one line as its query
- d61d1910  a local Windows terminal runs on Microsoft's ConPTY package instead of the
            inbox one; here the binaries are compiled into the client and installed in
            the user's cache folder (desktop/internal/localshell/conpty), not beside the
            executable, and a shell the inbox ConPTY hosts instead is logged

These Motty changes, older than the port, were in the parts left out at the port and are
taken now:

- fe2570d9  a paste that finds a picture and no text saves it and types its path;
- ed6db385  here the workbench saves it in the user's cache folder, for local terminals
- 3f7979e4  the cursor shape and thickness are chosen in the settings; here DECSCUSR 0
- 8a7476b6  also gives the chosen shape back, and the thickness applies to a shape a
            program asks for
